  "description": "Zorb finds out why the same 100 dollars buys a smaller basket of snacks: inflation, a rise in prices across the whole economy. Earth's central bank even aims for a little of it on purpose. Figures: the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (its 100-to-107 dollar example and the CPI for the 12 months ending September 2026) and the Federal Reserve's 2 percent goal, which it measures with a different price index (PCE).\n\nEducation, not financial advice.\n\n#Shorts #inflation #personalfinance",
